<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albany Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1754">1754</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Albany Congress was a meeting of delegates from seven British American colonies held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albany-new-york">Albany, New York</a>, in June and July 1754, as war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> loomed. It sought to renew the alliance with the Iroquois Confederacy and adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a>'s Albany Plan for a union of the colonies under a president-general. The colonial assemblies and the Crown rejected the plan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albany-congress.jpg" alt="Albany Congress" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allyn Cox · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albany_Congress.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
